{"format":"kards-original-reference","version":1,"id":"bf2862c99786956f","name":"card_event_motti_tactic","package":"/Game/Blueprints/Cards/Finland/events/card_event_motti_tactic","parent":"UBaseCardObject","card":{"title":"MOTTI TACTIC","text":"Destroy target unit. Add a copy of it to your hand.","flavorText":"\"Motti\" is Finnish military slang for completely encircling an enemy unit. The tactic, known as \"motitus,\" involves trapping the enemy. It's related to the idea of a small, manageable unit.\r\nFinnish forces used this tactic effectively in the Winter War and Continuation War, especially against Soviet mechanized units. Skilled Finnish troops would split the enemy columns into smaller segments in the forests, then attack from all sides. A \"motitus\" is a double envelopment maneuver, encircling enemies on a road with mobile troops. Despite being outnumbered, Finnish forces could immobilize larger enemy groups by dividing and surrounding them. If an encircled unit was too strong, it would be left to weaken due to a lack of supplies and ammunition. The Battle of Suomussalmi is a notable example where Finnish regiments surrounded and defeated two Soviet divisions and a tank brigade on a road.","faction":"Finland","type":"order","rarity":"Rare","cost":8,"operationCost":0,"attack":0,"defense":0},"defaults":{"UberGraphFrame":{},"Name":"card_event_motti_tactic","title":{"Namespace":"card_finland","Key":"card_event_motti_tactic_title","SourceString":"MOTTI TACTIC","LocalizedString":"MOTTI TACTIC"},"Type":"ETypeEnum::order","faction":"EFactionEnum::Finland","kredits":8,"Text":{"Namespace":"card_finland","Key":"card_event_motti_tactic_text","SourceString":"Destroy target unit. Add a copy of it to your hand.","LocalizedString":"Destroy target unit. Add a copy of it to your hand."},"flavorText":{"Namespace":"card_finland","Key":"card_event_motti_tactic_history","SourceString":"\"Motti\" is Finnish military slang for completely encircling an enemy unit. The tactic, known as \"motitus,\" involves trapping the enemy. It's related to the idea of a small, manageable unit.\r\nFinnish forces used this tactic effectively in the Winter War and Continuation War, especially against Soviet mechanized units. Skilled Finnish troops would split the enemy columns into smaller segments in the forests, then attack from all sides. A \"motitus\" is a double envelopment maneuver, encircling enemies on a road with mobile troops. Despite being outnumbered, Finnish forces could immobilize larger enemy groups by dividing and surrounding them. If an encircled unit was too strong, it would be left to weaken due to a lack of supplies and ammunition. The Battle of Suomussalmi is a notable example where Finnish regiments surrounded and defeated two Soviet divisions and a tank brigade on a road.","LocalizedString":"\"Motti\" is Finnish military slang for completely encircling an enemy unit. The tactic, known as \"motitus,\" involves trapping the enemy. It's related to the idea of a small, manageable unit.\r\nFinnish forces used this tactic effectively in the Winter War and Continuation War, especially against Soviet mechanized units. Skilled Finnish troops would split the enemy columns into smaller segments in the forests, then attack from all sides. A \"motitus\" is a double envelopment maneuver, encircling enemies on a road with mobile troops. Despite being outnumbered, Finnish forces could immobilize larger enemy groups by dividing and surrounding them. If an encircled unit was too strong, it would be left to weaken due to a lack of supplies and ammunition. The Battle of Suomussalmi is a notable example where Finnish regiments surrounded and defeated two Soviet divisions and a tank brigade on a road."},"rarity":"ERarityEnum::Rare","selectTargetOnPlayedFromHand":true,"cardSet":"ECardSetEnum::WinterWar","isInPermanentPool":true,"soundEnterPlay":{"ObjectName":"SoundWave'Anihilation_17'","ObjectPath":"kards/Content/Assets/Audio/Misc/OrdersFeb17/Anihilation_17.